        {
          "name": "George Bell",
          "role": "MSc Student at Queen Mary University of London",
          "description": "I am an MSc Biodiversity and Conservation student researching patterns in human-use species across different commercial scales, with a focus on variation in documented threats and conservation actions. I investigate how conservation attention differs across species subject to different levels and forms of human use. I completed a BSc in Wildlife and Practical Conservation from the University of Salford. My broader interests include macroecological patterns and their implications for conservation prioritisation and decision-making.",
